  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proyecto Titi efforts to expand our sustainable development programs to foster Cotton-Top Tamarin conservation Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Recipient will enter into a two-year cooperative agreement with the Wildlife Without Borders Latin America and Caribbean (WWB-LAC) program to expand its sustainable development activities (Tit Ventures) to 6 new rural communities where Proyecto Tit has been implementing the environmental education programs (CARTITILLA and Conservation Clubs) in local schools. The Recipient will: 1) conduct introductory sessions and training events on how the various Tit Ventures products can be made to reduce the extraction of forest resources in Cotton-top Tamarin habitat; 2) evaluate the implementation of conservation related behaviors between students who have adult family members who are involved in Tit Ventures and those who do not; and 3) provide follow-up training in conservation issues and marketing and sales to current Tit Ventures artisans.</narrative>
  </description>
